# Line endings: always store and check out text files with Unix-style (LF) endings.
#
# Why: git on Windows normally converts files to Windows-style (CRLF) endings
# when it checks them out. Prettier expects LF, so after a fresh checkout
# `npm run check` would fail on every file even though nothing changed.
# This rule keeps LF everywhere, on every computer.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are binary: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
